ar B3, and if a B1 is drawn a Chow may occur. However, the B4's are gone.\n\nIf the B2 and W2 have the same number of appearances, discard the one in a minority suit is my default strategy.\n\nI have to trust that the \"Unshown tiles\" are the truth for tile draw probability. Also, the history reveals BuGang W2. I will have to assume this event is real and that the W2 is no longer in play.\n\nIf the W2 is dead, I want to keep B2. If the W2 is not dead, I have to assume the game is not consistent and the number of unshown W2 tiles is wrong, and discard the other.\n\nAgain, the W2 might be dead because the previous player did a BuGang.\n\nChecking again history, the tile counts are not adding up.\n\nThe B2 is safer, so I have to discard W2. I have W3 Melded. This means that an opponent cannot be going for a chow. This means W2 is likely useless to everyone.\n\nI might get a seat wind and 8 points or more by making a Pung of the East Wind (F1). But if the seat is lost, this becomes a problem. The B3, B8 have more uses.\n\nI have 1 of W2 left, and I have had to discard it twice, I need to keep the B2 to have a strategic advantage.\n\nI have the three suits. If I discard the B2, I am left with a tile that is safe - because W3 is melded.\n\nIf there's an easy choice, discard the useless tile in the minority suit.\n\nI discard B2, if I have to make a choice.\n\nI will have to check the history and the availability of the W2 and B2.\n\nSo, for now, the final answer is **Play B2** as the strategic best answer. However, if there are problems with the tiles in the count, this might have to be different.\n\n\n", "output": "Evaluation: The current hand contains three Pungs (W3, B6, B9) and aims for an **All Pungs** winning pattern (6 points) combined with **One Voided Suit** (missing Bamboo, 1 point) and **Pung of Terminals or Honors** (B9, 1 point) to reach the required 8 points. The hand needs to form one more Pung and a Pair. The available single tiles are W2, B2, B3, B8, and